# Tool permission prompts: allow once, then deny (esc) and give feedback. Claude Code
# ends the turn on esc; the last two script turns share a reply so the scenario also
# completes when a target continues the turn after a denial.
name: tool-approval
size: 100x30
args: --permission-mode default "Create the marker file"
files: ../../../testdata/fixtures/12/app
script: scripts/tool-approval.json
parity: PD-01, PD-02, PD-08, PD-10, PD-13, TR-09, TR-27
---
ready
wait_for 30s touch parity-marker.txt
settle
checkpoint permission-prompt
keys enter
wait_for 30s Created parity-marker.txt.
settle
checkpoint allowed
type Clean up the scratch directory
keys enter
wait_for 30s rm -rf scratch-dir
settle
checkpoint second-prompt
keys esc
settle 5s
checkpoint denied
type Keep the scratch directory next time
keys enter
wait_for 30s Noted: keep the scratch directory.
settle
checkpoint feedback
